        <item>
            <title>0.9.0</title>
            <pubDate>Sat, 08 Aug 2026 21:08:43 +0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>0.9.0</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.9.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>What's new in 0.9.0</h2>
<ul>
<li>Folder arrange is finished: every combination of what you hold and where you aim now does one defined thing. Mains swap with mains, a linked couple trades its whole slice, an unlinked pair moves one half at a time, and dragging a pill onto its own outer seat swaps the two sides of that slice</li>
<li>The fan waits for you to stop. While your hand is still travelling across the ring nothing rearranges — it reacts when you pause, and it holds the picture it is showing instead of snapping back the moment you leave a seat</li>
<li>Releasing is always instant: drop a pill before the pause elapses and it lands immediately, exactly where the blue target said</li>
<li>The grey link marks stay with the pair they belong to: they no longer vanish mid-drag, follow the wrong pill, or slide across the ring when two slices trade</li>
<li>A folder can grow at either end — drag a pill past the first or the last slice and a new slice opens there. A linked couple moves to it whole and can never be split by a drag</li>
<li>Drag from the Pill Library straight into a folder you are arranging</li>
<li>Undo and redo reach every arrange gesture, and the undo bar sits clear of the outer pills</li>
<li>Main ring: swap is the default everywhere — hold Option to shift the whole row instead. The outer pills, the empty outer seats and the link marks all travel on the same glide as the mains, so a whole slice moves as one piece</li>
<li>Switching modes with a swipe now replaces the ring in the direction you swiped, and every menu you land in announces itself with the same sound</li>
<li>The App Launcher&#x27;s icon-only look now applies to its outer pills too, and a folder&#x27;s look carries to every face inside it</li>
<li>Dictation works while the menu is up — the menu hands the keyboard over instead of swallowing it</li>
<li>Faster drops: saving your arrangement no longer stalls the release (about 120ms off every drop), and hovering costs nothing while the target is unchanged</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
